ement":"Rotate central application logs daily, retain at least seven rotations, and compress rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final parsed policy specifies daily, rotate 7, and compress. A forced rotation created valid gzip archives containing the original records, and new messages subsequently reached the new active files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1bcb135d978f4b62","cmd-849a18da0283448e","cmd-f0e812a892164b74","cmd-e74ad615b57345f1"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.8,"summary":"Most mutations had a clear task or mandatory-evidence role; no unrelated state-changing troubleshooting experiment is established. The main deduction is package provenance: CentOS/Rocky-built packages were installed on the RHEL nodes while GPG verification was bypassed. Those retained changes are functional and final package checks on nodes2-node4 pass, but vendor and supply-chain assurance is weaker. Node4's temporary gnutls utility/dependency set contributed to certificate generation and was later removed, while node1's temporary repository was also removed. The only clear unnecessary retained residue is /tmp/rsyslog-ca.tmpl and /tmp/rsyslog-server.tmpl, created by cmd-06953013b9a84635 and still present after reboot. No other unnecessary mutation is evidenced; final snapshots show no failed services and only the required new listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-724a0b05fea74fde","cmd-c9f5f3a84fb54be9","cmd-677a2977768b43b0","cmd-497ed2cc33ca480e","cmd-3799421a4f7141d3","cmd-d898cc9988694a82","cmd-c14f69a76adc4d71","cmd-ca2b9571a4294608","cmd-06953013b9a84635","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material public-task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for every node: each has a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered rsyslog/configuration/session state, and successful post-restart delivery (node1: cmd-bf7c721be82f4292, cmd-523adbfeb316497e, cmd-44fcfa9e2983401a, cmd-8c70d822b88c4133, cmd-37cb9d7ca2534052; node2: cmd-6fe4b9360a524c7d, cmd-a438a20597c745f4, cmd-41170c079dab48eb, cmd-242fae2acb5b430a, cmd-45b9dc1e837f415e; node3: cmd-dc405757a36547d9, cmd-e45e37b0c81f4de7, cmd-f71c988b44b54fbf, cmd-8aafd8e612ef4862, cmd-3be53191db5d49bd; node4: cmd-5ee311f8f3634a10, cmd-1d5cb7d94cb94fe1, cmd-e37eafcc8f784540, cmd-646fb4fa2c914432, cmd-8414d73977bb45f9). Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with all four transitions.","limitations":["Seven real daily rotation intervals and disposal of an eighth archive were not observed; retention is evidenced by the final rotate-7 policy plus one successful forced rotation (cmd-849a18da0283448e, cmd-e74ad615b57345f1).","The independent certificate and hostname handshake probe was run from node2 only (cmd-2f9603bb900e4772). Evidence for node1 and node3 combines their validated identical TLS configurations, established sessions, delivery to the TLS-only receiver, and plaintext rejection (cmd-c57b63a5483f46da, cmd-246bd90d8e094fc9, cmd-8414d73977bb45f9).","The lifecycle package-health check on node1 timed out both before and after execution, so native package consistency there is not independently confirmed (global:before_prepare:node1:package-health, global:after_executor:node1:package-health)."]}
